24d9|n|The power or capacity of enduring; the act of enduring; endurance. ; The endurance of the presence or actions of objectionable persons, or of the expression of offensive opinions; toleration. ; The power possessed or acquired by some persons of bearing doses of medicine which in ordinary cases would prove injurious or fatal.	a:242d,71,8;19gl,49,3;ymm,31,4;kgh,16,3;1xnv,1,3~242d,71,8;ymm,31,4;1xnv,1,3;kgh,16,3;19gl,49,3	n:242i,93,4;2brw,64,7;2ay7,42,4;k8y,39,3;22wi,29,5~2brw,64,7;22wi,29,5;242i,93,4;2ay7,42,4;k8y,39,3	N:237u,48,9;db7,40,3~237u,48,9;db7,40,3
